      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": " \nWe can use the Euclidean algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20.\n\nTheir write the numbers on either side of the formula: \n\n1. **Number 1**: 20\n   **Number 2**: 12\n2. **Divide the larger number by the smaller and note the remainder:**\n   20 ÷ 12 = 1 remainder 8\n   20 = 1 × 12 + 8\n3. **Repeat the process with the number above and below until no remainder:**\n   12 ÷ 8 = 1 remainder 4\n   12 = 1 × 8 + 4\n   8 ÷ 4 = 2 remainder 0\n   8 = 2 × 4 + 0\n4. **When the remainder is 0, the GCD is the last non-zero remainder.**\n\nSo, the GCD of 20 and 12 is 4. Therefore, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is also 4. \n\n\\(\\boxed{4}\\)",
